ork: https://github.com/oracle/graalvm-reachability-metadata/tree/ai%2Fkimeta%2Fhuman-intervention%2Fissue-9764-library-update-request-org.apache.kafka-kafka-streams-4.3.1-4d1ed3f5\\n\\nThe run is classified as `test_generation_failed`, most likely during `explore/generate_tests()` before Gradle verification. No `4.3.1` test project, metadata, execution metrics, dynamic-access report, or Gradle output was preserved; the branch contains only failure-analysis logs. Additionally, `pi.log` reports `Pi RPC exited before completing prompt (exit code -2)`, and the generation transcript ends during preliminary documentation inspection, so the follow-up diagnosis was also interrupted.\\n\\nInspect:\\n- `human-intervention-logs/org.apache.kafka:kafka-streams:4.3.1/failure-analysis/pi.log`\\n- `human-intervention-logs/org.apache.kafka:kafka-streams:4.3.1/failure-analysis/pi-generation-2026-09-03T09-18-34-984249Z.log`\\n- Recover the original run logs, if available, from `logs/org.apache.kafka:kafka-streams:4.3.1/`.\\n\\nManual next steps:\\n1. Check the worker/process logs for the signal or timeout that caused the Pi RPC exit and recover any missing original test-generation transcript.\\n2. Create the `4.3.1` test project from the existing `3.6.0` suite, adapt it for Kafka Streams 4.3.1, and run `compileTestJava` followed by `javaTest`.\\n3. Once JVM tests pass, run the coordinate-scoped metadata/native test and dynamic-access reporting tasks, then generate the missing execution metrics.\", \"textSignature\": \"{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_01c1cd3808457d5b016a993d6321cc87d2ae34070182139473\\\",\\\"phase\\\":\\\"final_answer\\\"}\"}], \"api\": \"openai-codex-responses\", \"provider\": \"openai-codex\", \"model\": \"gpt-5.6-sol\", \"usage\": {\"input\": 4682, \"output\": 1438, \"cacheRead\": 148736, \"cacheWrite\": 0, \"reasoning\": 1034, \"totalTokens\": 154856, \"cost\": {\"input\": 0, \"output\": 0, \"cacheRead\": 0, \"cacheWrite\": 0, \"total\": 0}}, \"stopReason\": \"sto